{"requirements":[{"id":"swap-capacity-and-priority","requirement":"On node1, provide at least 512 MiB of active disk-backed swap, preferred over existing swap.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After correction, /swapfile supplied 532,472 KiB of active file-backed swap on the ext3 root disk at priority 100, while existing /dev/sda5 remained at priority -1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3fbf177ae78248c3","cmd-89fdc78fd8a841a6","cmd-6c5686c21403445b"]},{"id":"boot-persistence","requirement":"Ensure the added swap activates automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The fstab entry specifies /swapfile with priority 100. A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, temporarily interrupted connectivity, and the recovered node directly showed the swap active with the configured size and priority.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45308a9eed8f422e","cmd-89fdc78fd8a841a6","cmd-879a66c30fbe4099","cmd-02f4994392c74251","cmd-da1454f9b7774687","cmd-6c5686c21403445b","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were identical before and after execution. The implementation used utilities already present on the node, and package-health observations remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dea71a99cd134c5f","cmd-d2c4c2cad1d8447c","cmd-6c5686c21403445b","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"The final state is focused and healthy, with no package-health, socket, or /tmp residue changes. Two low-risk unnecessary mutations occurred: a 512 MiB swap file was first created and then initialized/activated, but this version was completely superseded by the corrected 520 MiB file. A rollback copy of fstab and a /var/tmp reboot log were also created for safety and restart diagnostics; their roles were related to the task, but cleanup was not demonstrated, so their retained status is uncertain. Temporary write-test files were explicitly removed. No broad, destructive, or security-weakening action is evident.","evidence_ids":["cmd-be6a127b09c84dff","cmd-31fa09eeedf14fd3","cmd-3fbf177ae78248c3","cmd-45308a9eed8f422e","cmd-89fdc78fd8a841a6","cmd-879a66c30fbe4099","cmd-6c5686c21403445b","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, an observed outage, a different post-restart boot ID, recovered runlevel/init state, writable storage, unchanged platform, persistent configuration, and active swap. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because this legacy image does not use systemd; runlevel, PID 1, storage write tests, swap state, and package health provide the available recovery evidence instead.","Neither the executor trace nor lifecycle snapshots establish whether /etc/fstab.before-swapfile and /var/tmp/benchmark-reboot.log were removed after successful verification.","There is no application or cluster workload on this single-node swap task to test beyond host, storage, boot-configuration, and swap recovery."]}
